course: dictionary
lesson: 12630
title: Dismount: getting off safely
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dismount means to get off something you were sitting on or riding, such as a horse, a bike or a motorbike. You can work this out from the clues in a sentence. «Cyclists dismount at the crossing and walk their bikes.» The sentence tells you what they do next: they walk, so dismount must mean getting off.
explain: Gymnasts dismount too. «The gymnast's dismount was perfect, and she landed softly on both feet.» Here a dismount is the last move that takes a gymnast off the apparatus (the equipment) and onto the floor. The landing clue tells you the meaning. The idea is the same: getting off.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «Cyclists get off at the crossing and walk their bikes» still make sense? Yes, so you have understood dismount correctly.
fact: Dismount means to get off a horse, bicycle or motorbike.
fact: A dismount is also a noun: it is the act of getting off, such as a gymnast's dismount.
fact: The other forms of the verb are dismounts, dismounted and dismounting.
fact: Mount is the opposite of dismount: to mount means to get up on or onto something.
fact: In computing, to dismount a drive means to disconnect it so it is safe to remove.
exercise: «She had to dismount before the steep hill.» What does dismount mean? | *Get off her horse or bike | Jump higher than the hill | Fall asleep on the grass | Ride faster up the slope
exercise: In gymnastics, what is a dismount? | Stretching before the routine starts | *The final move that takes a gymnast off the apparatus and onto the floor | A loud cheer from the crowd
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the opposite of dismount. | rider | bicycle | safely | *mount
test: «Cyclists dismount and walk their bikes past the school gate.» What must the cyclists do? | Lie down on the path | Ride faster through the gate | Ring the bell and keep riding | *Get off their bikes and walk
test: When a computer drive is dismounted, what has happened? | It has been filled with new files | All its files have been deleted | *It has been disconnected so it is safe to remove | It has been made faster
exam: Which word is a noun in «The gymnast's dismount was perfect.»? | perfect | *dismount | gymnast's | was
